{
  "dom_id": "question-166298",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "Find ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }f(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }f(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y=f(x)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14262363/assets/446f0fd704e09106f34a70fcbd3adb2806bfea13664114bd5d704fd3c8519001.png)\n\nAs $x$ decreases to $-\\infty $, the graph oscillates between the values $y=-4$ and $y=4$ indefinitely. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }f(x)={lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=DNE.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
